Glimwick adjusted his robes in the muggy Stranglethorn air, sweating profusely. Beside him, his succubus, Vex'ahlia, flicked her tail with disdain. "Keep the bloodsails off my wings, short one," she purred, vanishing into Lesser Invisibility. Glimwick grumbled, casting Corruption on a nearby troll. Vex'ahlia reappeared, landing a Lash of Pain. The troll turned on Glimwick. Vex'ahlia used Soothing Kiss, reducing her threat. "Handle it, darling," she smirked. Glimwick frantically tanked the troll, his health plummeting. He missed his voidwalker's Torment and Sacrifice shield. As a second troll added, Vex'ahlia Seduced it, but Glimwick was already dead, cursing his choice of demon. 

**Answer:** 
Voidwalkers hold aggro (Torment/Suffering) and tank, allowing the Warlock to freely cast and regenerate mana via Life Tap. The Succubus reduces her own threat (Soothing Kiss), forcing the Warlock to tank the mob, which causes massive downtime to recover health. [end of text]


